{"step_index":767,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T15:05:40Z","thinking":"All hosts successfully responded, indicating a fully functional passwordless connection across the cluster. The next step involves creating a playbook for auditing the WExtP topology, considering whether the filename should include \"topology\" or \"cluster\".\n\n\nThe initial phase retrieves backend server information, dynamically populating the inventory. The front-end audit will then analyze Nginx configuration files to map domains to back-end routes using an embedded parser. The back-end audit will gather PHP version information, examine PHP-FPM service states and listening ports and gather domain webroot information.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"---\n# ==============================================================================\n# Playbook: Audit WEXTP Cluster — Frontend/Backend Topology & BE Deep Dive\n# ==============================================================================\n# 1. Phase 1: Queries KeePass server pool via playbooks/kdbx-pool.yml for all\n#             trp-wextp-be nodes and dynamically registers inventory groups.\n# 2. Phase 2: Audits Front-Ends (fe1, fe2, fe3) to discover which Backend nodes\n#             (and ports) each hosted domain connects to via fastcgi_pass/proxy_pass.\n# 3. Phase 3: Audits Back-Ends (be1 to be11) for:\n#             - PHP CLI version, active PHP-FPM services & listening pool ports\n#             - ProxySQL service status, version, config & listening ports\n#             - Root directories (/var/www/*) and match against routed domains.\n# 4. Phase 4: Consolidates findings into aligned cross-cluster topology tables.\n#\n# Usage:\n#   ansible-playbook -i inventory/hosts.ini playbooks/audit-wextp-topology.yml\n# ==============================================================================\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Phase 1: Query Server Pool for Backends via kdbx-pool\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n- name: \"Phase 1a - Query Server Pool for Backends via kdbx-pool\"\n  ansible.builtin.import_playbook: kdbx-pool.yml\n  vars:\n    search: \"trp-wextp-be\"\n\n- name: \"Phase 1b - Ensure WEXTP Dynamic Inventory Groups from Pool\"\n  hosts: localhost\n  connection: local\n  gather_facts: false\n  tasks:\n    - name: Load server pool cache\n      ansible.builtin.slurp:\n        src: \"{{ playbook_dir }}/../inventory/server_pool.json\"\n      register: _pool_raw\n      failed_when: false\n\n    - name: Dynamically register backend hosts if not present\n      ansible.builtin.add_host:\n        name: \"{{ item.title.split()[0] }}\"\n        ansible_host: \"{{ item.primary_ip | default(item.ips[0]) }}\"\n        ansible_port: \"{{ item.port | default(30) }}\"\n        ansible_user: \"koby-bowser-ansible\"\n        ansible_ssh_common_args: \"-o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new\"\n        groups:\n          - wextp_backends\n      loop: \"{{ (_pool_raw.content | b64decode | from_json).servers | selectattr('title', 'search', '^trp-wextp-be[0-9]+') | selectattr('group', 'search', 'WEXTP$') | unique(attribute='title') | list }}\"\n      when: _pool_raw.content is defined\n\n    - name: Dynamically register frontend hosts if not present\n      ansible.builtin.add_host:\n        name: \"{{ item.title.split()[0] }}\"\n        ansible_host: \"{{ item.primary_ip | default(item.ips[0]) }}\"\n        ansible_port: \"{{ item.port | default(30) }}\"\n        ansible_user: \"koby-bowser-ansible\"\n        ansible_ssh_common_args: \"-o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new\"\n        groups:\n          - wextp_frontends\n      loop: \"{{ (_pool_raw.content | b64decode | from_json).servers | selectattr('title', 'search', '^trp-wextp-fe[0-9]+') | selectattr('group', 'search', 'WEXTP$') | unique(attribute='title') | list }}\"\n      when: _pool_raw.content is defined\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Phase 2: Audit Front-Ends — Extract Domain to Backend Connections\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n- name: \"Phase 2 - Audit Front-Ends (FE to BE Topology)\"\n  hosts: wextp_frontends\n  gather_facts: true\n  become: true\n  become_method: ansible.builtin.sudo\n  vars:\n    ansible_ssh_common_args: \"-o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new\"\n\n  tasks:\n    - name: Inspect Nginx configuration on Front-Ends\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        argv:\n          - /usr/bin/python3\n          - -c\n          - |\n            import glob, re, os, json, socket\n\n            upstreams = {}\n            # 1. Parse all upstreams in /etc/nginx/omt/*.conf, conf.d/*.conf, nginx.conf\n            conf_paths = glob.glob(\"/etc/nginx/omt/*.conf\") + glob.glob(\"/etc/nginx/conf.d/*.conf\") + [\"/etc/nginx/nginx.conf\"]\n            for cp in conf_paths:\n                if not os.path.isfile(cp):\n                    continue\n                try:\n                    with open(cp) as f:\n                        content = f.read()\n                    for m in re.finditer(r\"upstream\\s+([a-zA-Z0-9_\\-]+)\\s*\\{([^}]+)\\}\", content):\n                        up_name = m.group(1)\n                        body = m.group(2)\n                        servers = []\n                        for line in body.splitlines():\n                            line = line.strip()\n                            if line.startswith(\"server \") and not line.startswith(\"#\"):\n                                parts = line.replace(\";\", \"\").split()\n                                if len(parts) >= 2:\n                                    target = parts[1]\n                                    node = target.split(\":\")[0]\n                                    port = target.split(\":\")[1] if \":\" in target else \"80\"\n                                    servers.append({\"target\": target, \"node\": node, \"port\": port})\n                        if servers:\n                            upstreams[up_name] = servers\n                except Exception:\n                    pass\n\n            # 2. Parse server blocks in sites-enabled\n            def parse_nginx_file(filepath):\n                try:\n                    with open(filepath) as f:\n                        content = f.read()\n                except Exception:\n                    return []\n\n                # Remove comments\n                lines = [l for l in content.splitlines() if not l.strip().startswith(\"#\")]\n                clean_text = \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n                blocks = []\n                idx = 0\n                while True:\n                    m = re.search(r\"(?:^|\\s)server\\s*\\{(?!\\s*name)\", clean_text[idx:])\n                    if not m:\n                        break\n                    start = idx + m.end()\n                    depth = 1\n                    pos = start\n                    while pos < len(clean_text) and depth > 0:\n                        if clean_text[pos] == \"{\":\n                            depth += 1\n                        elif clean_text[pos] == \"}\":\n                            depth -= 1\n                        pos += 1\n                    server_body = clean_text[start:pos-1]\n                    idx = pos\n\n                    # Server names\n                    s_names = []\n                    for sn in re.findall(r\"server_name\\s+([^;]+);\", server_body):\n                        s_names.extend([x.strip() for x in sn.split() if x.strip()])\n\n                    # Roots\n                    roots = re.findall(r\"(?:^|\\s)root\\s+([^;]+);\", server_body)\n                    doc_root = roots[0].strip() if roots else None\n\n                    # Passes\n                    passes = re.findall(r\"(?:fastcgi_pass|proxy_pass)\\s+([^;]+);\", server_body)\n                    targets = list(set([p.strip() for p in passes if not p.strip().startswith(\"$\")]))\n\n                    # Listen ports\n                    listens = re.findall(r\"listen\\s+([^;]+);\", server_body)\n                    ports = []\n                    for l in listens:\n                        p = l.strip().split()[0]\n                        if p not in ports:\n                            ports.append(p)\n\n                    if s_names and targets:\n                        blocks.append({\n                            \"conf\": os.path.basename(filepath),\n                            \"domains\": [d for d in s_names if d != \"_\"],\n                            \"ports\": ports,\n                            \"root\": doc_root,\n                            \"targets\": targets\n                        })\n                return blocks\n\n            routes = []\n            for p in sorted(glob.glob(\"/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/*\")):\n                if os.path.isfile(p):\n                    for b in parse_nginx_file(p):\n                        if not b[\"domains\"]:\n                            continue\n                        # Resolve target to backend nodes\n                        resolved_backends = []\n                        target_names = []\n                        for t in b[\"targets\"]:\n                            target_names.append(t)\n                            if t in upstreams:\n                                for s in upstreams[t]:\n                                    resolved_backends.append(s)\n                            else:\n                                # direct IP or host\n                                clean_t = t.replace(\"http://\", \"\").replace(\"https://\", \"\").split(\"/\")[0]\n                                if \":\" in clean_t:\n                                    h, pt = clean_t.split(\":\")\n                                    resolved_backends.append({\"target\": clean_t, \"node\": h, \"port\": pt})\n                                else:\n                                    resolved_backends.append({\"target\": clean_t, \"node\": clean_t, \"port\": \"80\"})\n\n                        # Deduplicate backends\n                        unique_bes = []\n                        seen = set()\n                        for be in resolved_backends:\n                            key = f\"{be['node']}:{be['port']}\"\n                            if key not in seen:\n                                seen.add(key)\n                                unique_bes.append(be)\n\n                        routes.append({\n                            \"conf\": b[\"conf\"],\n                            \"domains\": b[\"domains\"],\n                            \"ports\": b[\"ports\"],\n                            \"root\": b[\"root\"],\n                            \"target_pools\": target_names,\n                            \"backends\": unique_bes\n                        })\n\n            print(json.dumps({\n                \"fe\": socket.gethostname(),\n                \"routes\": routes,\n                \"upstreams\": upstreams\n            }))\n      register: _fe_audit_raw\n      changed_when: false\n\n    - name: Store parsed frontend routing facts\n      ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n        fe_audit: \"{{ _fe_audit_raw.stdout | from_json }}\"\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Phase 3: Audit Back-Ends — PHP Versions, ProxySQL, Webroots\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n- name: \"Phase 3 - Audit Back-Ends (PHP, ProxySQL, Webroots)\"\n  hosts: wextp_backends\n  gather_facts: true\n  become: true\n  become_method: ansible.builtin.sudo\n  vars:\n    ansible_ssh_common_args: \"-o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new\"\n\n  tasks:\n    - name: Inspect PHP engines, ProxySQL, and webroots on Backend\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        argv:\n          - /usr/bin/python3\n          - -c\n          - |\n            import subprocess, os, re, glob, socket, json\n\n            res = {}\n            res[\"host\"] = socket.gethostname()\n\n            # 1. PHP CLI version\n            php_cli = \"\"\n            try:\n                p = subprocess.run([\"php\", \"-v\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n                if p.returncode == 0:\n                    php_cli = p.stdout.splitlines()[0].strip()\n            except Exception:\n                php_cli = \"not installed\"\n            res[\"php_cli\"] = php_cli\n\n            # Active FPM services\n            fpm_services = []\n            try:\n                p = subprocess.run([\"systemctl\", \"list-units\", \"--type=service\", \"php*\", \"--state=running\", \"--no-legend\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n                for line in p.stdout.splitlines():\n                    parts = line.split()\n                    if parts:\n                        fpm_services.append(parts[0])\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            res[\"fpm_services\"] = fpm_services\n\n            # Listening PHP ports\n            php_ports = []\n            try:\n                p = subprocess.run([\"ss\", \"-tulpn\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n                for line in p.stdout.splitlines():\n                    if \"php\" in line:\n                        parts = line.split()\n                        if len(parts) >= 5:\n                            local_addr = parts[4]\n                            port = local_addr.split(\":\")[-1]\n                            php_ports.append(port)\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            res[\"php_ports\"] = sorted(list(set(php_ports)), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else 0)\n\n            # 2. ProxySQL inspection\n            proxysql = {}\n            try:\n                p = subprocess.run([\"systemctl\", \"is-active\", \"proxysql\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n                proxysql[\"service\"] = p.stdout.strip()\n            except Exception:\n                proxysql[\"service\"] = \"unknown\"\n\n            try:\n                p = subprocess.run([\"proxysql\", \"--version\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n                proxysql[\"version\"] = p.stdout.strip()\n            except Exception:\n                proxysql[\"version\"] = \"N/A\"\n\n            proxysql[\"config_exists\"] = os.path.exists(\"/etc/proxysql.cnf\")\n            proxysql[\"config_size\"] = os.path.getsize(\"/etc/proxysql.cnf\") if proxysql[\"config_exists\"] else 0\n\n            psql_ports = []\n            try:\n                p = subprocess.run([\"ss\", \"-tulpn\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n                for line in p.stdout.splitlines():\n                    if \"proxysql\" in line:\n                        parts = line.split()\n                        if len(parts) >= 5:\n                            local_addr = parts[4]\n                            port = local_addr.split(\":\")[-1]\n                            psql_ports.append(port)\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            proxysql[\"ports\"] = sorted(list(set(psql_ports)), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else 0)\n            res[\"proxysql\"] = proxysql\n\n            # 3. Webroot directories in /var/www/\n            webroots = []\n            if os.path.isdir(\"/var/www\"):\n                for item in sorted(os.listdir(\"/var/www\")):\n                    full = os.path.join(\"/var/www\", item)\n                    if not item.startswith(\".\"):\n                        is_link = os.path.islink(full)\n                        real = os.path.realpath(full) if is_link else full\n                        is_dir = os.path.isdir(full)\n                        if is_dir:\n                            webroots.append({\n                                \"name\": item,\n                                \"path\": full,\n                                \"is_symlink\": is_link,\n                                \"target\": real if is_link else None,\n                            })\n            res[\"webroots\"] = webroots\n\n            print(json.dumps(res))\n      register: _be_audit_raw\n      changed_when: false\n\n    - name: Store parsed backend audit facts\n      ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n        be_audit: \"{{ _be_audit_raw.stdout | from_json }}\"\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Phase 4: Consolidated Cluster Topology & Audit Reporting\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n- name: \"Phase 4 - Consolidated Cluster Topology & Audit Reporting\"\n  hosts: localhost\n  connection: local\n  gather_facts: false\n  tasks:\n    - name: Display Host-by-Host Backend Health Summary\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg: |\n          ====================================================================================================\n          BACKEND NODE AUDIT: {{ item }}\n          ====================================================================================================\n          {% set be = hostvars[item].be_audit | default({}) %}\n          * Hostname         : {{ be.host | default(item) }} ({{ hostvars[item].ansible_host | default('N/A') }})\n          * PHP CLI          : {{ be.php_cli | default('N/A') }}\n          * Active PHP-FPM   : {{ be.fpm_services | default([]) | join(', ') if be.fpm_services else 'None running' }}\n          * Listening Ports  : {{ be.php_ports | default([]) | join(', ') if be.php_ports else 'None' }}\n          * ProxySQL Service : {{ be.proxysql.service | default('N/A') | upper }} ({{ be.proxysql.version | default('N/A') }})\n          * ProxySQL Config  : {{ '/etc/proxysql.cnf (' ~ be.proxysql.config_size ~ ' bytes)' if (be.proxysql.config_exists | default(false)) else 'NOT FOUND' }}\n          * ProxySQL Ports   : {{ be.proxysql.ports | default([]) | join(', ') if be.proxysql.ports else 'None' }}\n          * Hosted Webroots  : {{ be.webroots | default([]) | length }} root directories in /var/www/\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n      loop: \"{{ groups['wextp_backends'] | sort }}\"\n\n    - name: Display Front-End to Back-End Domain Routing Topology Table\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg: |\n          ========================================================================================================================================================================\n          WEXTP TOPOLOGY: FRONT-END TO BACK-END DOMAIN ROUTING TABLE\n          ========================================================================================================================================================================\n          {{ '%-15s' | format('FRONT-END') }} | {{ '%-40s' | format('HOSTED DOMAIN(S)') }} | {{ '%-22s' | format('UPSTREAM POOL') }} | {{ '%-35s' | format('TARGET BACKEND(S)') }} | {{ '%-12s' | format('PORT(S)') }} | {{ '%-25s' | format('FE ROOT DIRECTORY') }}\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          {% for fe_name in groups['wextp_frontends'] | sort %}\n          {% set fe = hostvars[fe_name].fe_audit | default({}) %}\n          {% for r in fe.routes | default([]) %}\n          {% set be_nodes = [] %}\n          {% set be_ports = [] %}\n          {% for b in r.backends | default([]) %}\n          {% set _ = be_nodes.append(b.node) %}\n          {% set _ = be_ports.append(b.port) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n          {{ '%-15s' | format(fe_name) }} | {{ '%-40s' | format((r.domains | join(', ')) | truncate(40, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-22s' | format((r.target_pools | join(', ')) | truncate(22, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-35s' | format((be_nodes | unique | join(', ')) | truncate(35, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-12s' | format((be_ports | unique | join(',')) | truncate(12, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-25s' | format((r.root or 'None') | truncate(25, True, '...')) }}\n          {% endfor %}\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          {% endfor %}\n          ========================================================================================================================================================================\n\n    - name: Display Back-End Infrastructure, PHP & ProxySQL Summary Table\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg: |\n          ========================================================================================================================================================================\n          WEXTP INFRASTRUCTURE: BACK-END NODES, PHP ENGINES & PROXYSQL STATUS\n          ========================================================================================================================================================================\n          {{ '%-16s' | format('BACKEND NODE') }} | {{ '%-16s' | format('IP ADDRESS') }} | {{ '%-18s' | format('PHP CLI') }} | {{ '%-35s' | format('ACTIVE PHP-FPM SERVICES') }} | {{ '%-28s' | format('LISTENING PHP PORTS') }} | {{ '%-16s' | format('PROXYSQL STATUS') }} | {{ '%-14s' | format('PROXYSQL PORTS') }} | {{ '%-8s' | format('WEBROOTS') }}\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          {% for be_name in groups['wextp_backends'] | sort %}\n          {% set be = hostvars[be_name].be_audit | default({}) %}\n          {% set ip = hostvars[be_name].ansible_host | default('N/A') %}\n          {% set php_v = (be.php_cli.split()[1] if (be.php_cli and be.php_cli.split() | length > 1) else (be.php_cli or 'N/A')) %}\n          {% set fpm_str = (be.fpm_services | default([]) | join(', ')) %}\n          {% set ports_str = (be.php_ports | default([]) | join(',')) %}\n          {% set psql_stat = (be.proxysql.service | default('N/A') | upper) %}\n          {% set psql_pts = (be.proxysql.ports | default([]) | join(',')) %}\n          {% set roots_cnt = (be.webroots | default([]) | length | string ~ ' roots') %}\n          {{ '%-16s' | format(be_name) }} | {{ '%-16s' | format(ip) }} | {{ '%-18s' | format(php_v | truncate(18, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-35s' | format(fpm_str | truncate(35, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-28s' | format(ports_str | truncate(28, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-16s' | format(psql_stat | truncate(16, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-14s' | format(psql_pts | truncate(14, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-8s' | format(roots_cnt) }}\n          {% endfor %}\n          ========================================================================================================================================================================\n","Description":"Add audit-wextp-topology playbook to analyze FE-to-BE routing, PHP versions, ProxySQL and webroots","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/audit-wextp-topology.yml","toolAction":"Writing audit-wextp-topology playbook","toolSummary":"Write topology playbook"}}]}
